# One of two representations of cumulative mechanical motor-shaft position.
#
# Tick mode preserves integer counter increments from Hall sensors, encoders,
# and ESC tachometers. Floating-point mode is for sources natively reporting
# mechanical revolutions. Do not convert an exact counter into float32 when
# tick mode is available, because float32 loses fractional resolution at large
# cumulative positions.
#
# The union tag is one bit: 0 = ticks, 1 = revolutions.

@union

MotorPositionTicks ticks
float32 revolutions
